Package: conch-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Conch contributors <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/njdaniel/conch
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Description: Conch desktop app
 The Conch chat client as a desktop app (Electron), with the bundled
 conch-voice helper for push-to-talk voice. It talks to a conchd server over
 its public API and keeps its data per user. Run it as conch-desktop.
 .
 It needs AppArmor 4 and a system of the Ubuntu 24.04 class: the package
 ships an AppArmor profile (abi 4.0) that lets the app create the user
 namespace its sandbox needs. Where the profile cannot load and unprivileged
 user namespaces are restricted, the app will not start.
 .
 The package changes nothing about keyboard-device access: the talk-key
 permission is an explicit step the app shows, never done by installing.
